# Bounded public cache

Unauthenticated list routes must not store arbitrary `search`, `actor`, or pagination combinations in Redis. A client can otherwise fill or churn Redis with full KEV/NVD payloads.

Redis-cache only a small, explicit allowlist (`cache_if`). Typical `/kev` bounds: `page <= 10`, `per_page == 25`, empty `search` and `actor`. Exact repeats of rejected variants may use the bounded in-process LRU (`LOCAL_REPEAT_CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES`), not a new Redis key.

Low-cardinality windows (for example `/kev/recent?days=`) share one max-window Redis key and filter in process. Do not create one key per user parameter.

```python
# ❌ BAD — every search/actor/page lands in Redis
@cache(timeout=120, query_string=canonical_all_kev_query_items)

# ✅ GOOD — Redis only for bounded variants
@cache(
    timeout=120,
    query_string=canonical_all_kev_query_items,
    cache_if=should_cache_all_kev,
)
```
